<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">al-lŭbesco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adl-</span></b> ), ĕre,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.</i>
			[lubet]. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> With
				dat., <i>to be pleasing to</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illa basiare volenti promptis saviolis
					adlubescebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 7, p. 192, 40</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, p.
			10</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hercle vero jam adlubescit (femina) primulum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 4, 2, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adlubescere aquis,</span>”
				<i>to find pleasure in</i>, <i>to drink with
					pleasure</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, p. 218, 27</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
